From ec9cbad32a087b243d8d4b02c661c13974758a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:35:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ZipPass: StreetPass Games overview (Build 136)

ZipPass > StreetPass Games... shows every game's StreetPass box without
starting System Settings: game name and icon (from the game list, found
through sysdata/cecIds.txt or the box's title ID), StreetPass ID, inbox
and outbox counts (with ZipPass messages still waiting for room), last
opened, last received, and a status that points out half-made boxes
(missing MBoxInfo, inbox or outbox, a folder not in MBoxList, or a
listed box without a folder).

Per game: a Share tick, Open Box Folder (also on double-click), Empty
Inbox and Remove StreetPass Data (folder deleted and taken out of
MBoxList____, like System Settings does). For the whole folder: Open CEC
Folder and Zip CEC Folder (every file and folder, under CEC/ in the
zip). Viewing works while a game runs; emptying and removing only when
no game is running.

Unticked games are kept on this console: <user>/zippass/not_shared.txt
lists them, and ZipPass export now leaves them out. The built-in NetPass
client will use the same list.

Core: listStreetPassBoxes, clearStreetPassInbox, removeStreetPassBox,
zipStreetPassFolder, isStreetPassShared/setStreetPassShared in
zip_pass.cpp (under the ZipPass lock), with tests.

